1]Explain Optional in java ?

	->Optional is a class introduced in java8 in the java.util package,it represents a value that may or may not
	be present,it helps us handle absent values explicitly and reduces direct null checks
	->Optional is an inbuilt class so it has inbuilt methods like of(),ofNullable(),isPresent(),ifPresentOrElse()
	->It is commonly used as a method return type when a result may be absent.
